# ── Per-machine config (gitignored) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Defence in depth: local.properties is gitignored, but secret-scanners
# walk the filesystem. Repeating the exclusion here avoids re-flagging
# every audit run.
**/local.properties

# ── Single-purpose security primitives ──────────────────────────────────
# These files exist ONLY to implement a specific cryptographic / path
# defence primitive that triggers a generic rule by design. Inline
# `nosemgrep:` markers are in place for local devs running Semgrep
# directly (verified suppressing under `--config=auto`), but the
# YancoXplorer audit runner ignores them (audit 2026-05-16 still
# reported pre-existing markers on subtitle-extractor.ts and
# AndroidManifest.xml). Wholesale path exclusion is acceptable here
# because each file is tightly scoped (≤90 lines, single
# responsibility) — adding unrelated code to any of them would be a
# code-organisation smell that review should catch independently.
# AUDIT_NOTES.md cross-references each entry below.
#
# safe-path.ts IS the path-traversal guard (`confinePath` /
# `tryConfinePath`). Every `path.resolve` / `path.relative` call here
# is the defence itself.
src/main/utils/safe-path.ts
#
# BackupCipher.android.kt: AES-256-GCM with a fresh 96-bit random IV
# per call (NIST SP 800-38D §8.2.1). Semgrep flags every GCM usage as
# a review tripwire; the IV invariant is met by construction.
packages/shared/src/androidMain/kotlin/com/yancotv/shared/backup/BackupCipher.android.kt
#
# AndroidKeystoreCredentialStore.kt: AES/GCM where the Keystore manages
# the IV (`cipher.iv` read post-init). Same review-tripwire rationale.
packages/shared/src/androidMain/kotlin/com/yancotv/shared/sources/AndroidKeystoreCredentialStore.kt
